  "schema": "power.model.v1",
  "description": "Sampled sensor-driven dual-clutch research state machine on the complete seven-forward/reverse, three-output power path. The controller owns all ten drive/selector commands, preselects an unloaded target path, confirms physical synchronization and lock before declaring an active gear, and uses bounded release/engagement ramps with an explicit torque interruption. Neutral abort, synchronization timeout, moving direction-change block and new-request recovery are observable. Requested gear is an integral state_code input, distinct from confirmed actual gear. Engine torque coordination, fault diagnostics beyond these states, detailed dog/baulk-ring and clutch actuator dynamics, full OEM calibration and complete ECU/TCU remain open. All parameters are unverified.",
